            "review_text": "SteadfastInDuty\nSingapore, Singapore4 contributions\n0\nReally nice experience of Vietnamese street food\nDec 2012 • Couples\nNot being able to speak Vietnamese was a major obstacle from visiting the various street food stalls that commonly line the streets of Da Nang. However, Mappi Do's owner, Thao, can speak really good English and she helped us in ordering the frog porridge. Sitting along the street and doing what the locals do was a very interesting experience... The ambience was great, the frog porridge was unique, delicious and cheaply priced (about 20,000 to 30,000 VND)! :) We also had a lot of fun talking with Thao and learning more about Da Nang... One should definitely give this place a go to experience local culture and cuisine! \n\nNote that this is a night-time stall and opens from 6pm to 10pm...\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 5, 2012",
